  "method": "46 fresh subprocess cases:6explicit constructor-only and14supported public tail(1).collect actions comparing independent original baseline/current packages;22rows/partition scaling cases and4widepayloadcases comparing an independent intermediate pre-sharing package/current. Warm eval(0), time only supported action, verify output values; one run percase.15sconstructor/30saction caps;macOSRSSbytes includesruntime/preparation/localization. Finalcurrent action/constructor/scaling and paired wide cases rerun sequentially after build/test gates completed.",
  "limitations": [
    "Single-run timings are noisy; no universal speedup claim. Constructor cases isolate marking and do not claim arbitrary shared-DAG execution is linear.",
    "Original baseline mean,array32,andgroup outputs failed assertions; earlier100000rows/64partitions sum also failed. These are the diagnosed nondeterministic ordering defect; failed action timings are unavailable. All measured current actions passed.",
    "Stable source ordinals are attached before window sort/hash redistribution. The narrow Vail source caller guarantees one ordered physical stream per logical source partition; tail numbers a single ordered concatenation. Checked counters belong to individual execute streams.",
    "The generic finisher delegates actual UDAF merge/evaluate, without trusting its name/state shape; per-row accumulator work remains for generic reducers. Plain sums/counts retain native window execution.",
    "Scalar carry snapshots remain one-row at the public finisher boundary; relational joins can still repeat carry payloads. Complete grouped/array prefix snapshots remain costly.",
    "The sharing fix removes optimizer expansion of a common parallel producer across partition views. Scan-tail full-count windows and prefix sort/join paths may still materialize row data; no universal streaming-memory bound is claimed.",
    "Two inventory tests require the absent external Hail checkout and are excluded; dependency implementations remain untouched."
  ],
